# cmd.exe parses a batch file line by line, and its handling of labels (`goto`, `call :label`) and
# of parenthesised blocks is unreliable when lines end with LF only. Both scripts here stop every
# run through `call :fail` and a block, so a Linux-authored checkout has to arrive on Windows with
# CRLF. The blobs stay LF-normalised, so this changes no diff and no tooling output on other
# platforms — only what `git checkout` writes into the working tree.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
